UPDATE companies SET description='Tele-Fonika Cable Americas Corp. is headquartered in Lockport, Illinois. The company began operations in the American markets in 1987 as the distribution arm of the Poland-based TFKable Group. No founders are named; it operates as a subsidiary of the group.

The company supplies a broad portfolio of cables and accessories across North and South America, including high and extra-high voltage cables, medium voltage cables with EPR and XLPE insulation, industrial cables, mining cables, welding cables, flexible cords, submersible pump cables, and stage lighting cables. The Americas Corp notes it operates several production lines equipped for continuous vulcanization, twisting, and braiding, enabling precise cable manufacturing with full quality control at each stage. Specific facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not disclosed.

Its customers span the energy sector—power grid operators and offshore wind farm developers such as the Baltic Sea projects Bałtyk 2, Bałtyk 3, Baltica 2, and Baltic Power—as well as mining, industrial, welding, submersible pump, and stage lighting applications. Sales are conducted through a network of authorized distributors, international sales agents, and national sales representatives.

The TFKable Group emphasizes quality assurance through its accredited Quality Control Department Laboratory in Bydgoszcz (Polish Centre for Accreditation per PN-EN ISO/IEC 17025:2018) and advanced testing at the Extra-High Speed Laboratory in Krakow, where Monospiral Wheel, Festoon, and Drag Chain apparatuses verify cable flexibility, durability, and reliability under dynamic loads. The group also offers the TFPowerPack Mobile mobile energy storage system for emergency and maintenance power needs.', certifications=ARRAY['PN-EN ISO/IEC 17025:2018-02','ICEA S-75-381','NEMA WC58']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable distribution across North and South America", "Sales network management (authorized distributors, agents, representatives)", "Continuous vulcanization", "Twisting and braiding", "Quality control testing (via group laboratories)", "Custom cable solutions"], "industries": ["Energy (power grid)", "Offshore wind", "Mining", "Industrial", "Welding", "Submersible pump", "Stage lighting", "Electromobility", "Public transport", "Urban mobility", "Transport infrastructure"], "materials": ["Copper (soft drawn, extra flexible, stranded, tinned)", "EPR insulation", "XLPE insulation", "Polyamide threads", "Polypropylene (PP)", "Thermoplastic Elastomer (TPE-E)", "EPDM rubber", "Semi-conductive tape", "Composite tinned copper/polyamide braid", "Rubber-filled binder tape", "Bare or coated copper", "Fiber optic modules"], "equipment": ["Continuous vulcanization lines", "Twisting machines", "Braiding machines", "Monospiral Wheel test apparatus", "Festoon test apparatus", "Drag Chain test apparatus", "Extra-High Speed Laboratory (Krakow)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Documented deliveries to power grid operators", "Positive results from production process audits", "Quality Control Laboratory accredited to PN-EN ISO/IEC 17025:2018", "Advanced dynamic cable testing (Monospiral Wheel, Festoon, Drag Chain)", "TFPowerPack Mobile mobile energy storage for off-grid applications"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lockport, Illinois -> db", "Operations began in 1987 -> /about-us", "Distribution company of TFKable Group -> /about-us", "Product range: high/extra-high voltage, medium voltage, industrial, mining, welding, flexible cords, submersible pump, stage lighting cables -> /about-us", "Sales through authorized distributors, international agents, national representatives -> /about-us", "Production lines: continuous vulcanization, twisting, braiding -> /about-us", "Quality Control Laboratory in Bydgoszcz accredited per PN-EN ISO/IEC 17025:2018 -> /", "Extra-High Speed Laboratory in Krakow with Monospiral Wheel, Festoon, Drag Chain tests -> /", "Offshore wind farm deliveries: Ba\u0142tyk 2, Ba\u0142tyk 3, Baltica 2, Baltic Power -> /", "TFPowerPack Mobile mobile energy storage system -> /", "Certifications: ICEA S-75-381, NEMA WC58 -> /", "Materials: copper, EPR, XLPE, polyamide, PP, TPE-E, EPDM, etc. -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Tele-Fonika Cable Americas Corp. is the distribution company of the TFKable Group.", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tele-fonika-cable-americas-crp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='TerraSteel Furniture Design LLC operates from Bend, Oregon, where it was founded by Kirk Casey. The company is now owned by Justin Penfield, who serves as owner, designer, and fabricator. Penfield, originally from Pennsylvania, moved to Central Oregon in 2012 and joined TerraSteel before taking ownership.

The shop produces custom and handcrafted furniture ranging from modern to traditional styles. Using on-site woodworking, welding, and metal fabrication, the team works with steel, non-endangered exotic hardwoods, and reclaimed local timbers. Product lines include live-edge tables, custom knife blocks, wine racks, and the ARTifacts series.

TerraSteel serves residential clients, commercial spaces, restaurants, interior designers, and builders. Examples include custom knife blocks for home kitchens, live-edge dining tables for restaurants, and built-in pieces for commercial interiors. The company also collaborates directly with interior designers and builders on project-specific furniture.

The company emphasizes the “marriage of design and function,” with attention to detail at every step from concept to reality. Penfield notes that owning TerraSteel allows him to fuse fabrication, woodworking, and creative materials daily. The use of sustainable, non-endangered woods and reclaimed timber reflects a commitment to responsible material sourcing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Woodworking", "Welding", "Metal fabrication", "Custom furniture design", "Live edge furniture fabrication"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Restaurants", "Interior Designers", "Builders"], "materials": ["Steel", "Non-endangered exotic hardwoods", "Reclaimed local timbers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["On-site woodworking, welding, and metal fabrication", "Use of non-endangered exotic hardwoods and reclaimed local timbers", "Custom furniture for residential, commercial, and restaurant settings", "Award-winning knife block design", "Direct collaboration with interior designers and builders"], "facts_used": ["Company name: Terrasteel Furniture Design LLC -> db", "Headquarters: Bend, Oregon -> db", "Description: custom and handcrafted furniture using steel, exotic hardwoods, reclaimed timbers -> db", "Founder: Kirk Casey -> /about-us", "Current owner: Justin Penfield (Owner/Designer/Fabricator) -> /about-us", "Employee: Jut McDaniels (Fabricator) -> /about-us", "Processes: woodworking, welding, fabrication on-site -> /", "Materials: steel, non-endangered exotic hardwoods, reclaimed local timbers -> /", "Product lines: custom knife blocks, wine racks, live edge collection, ARTifacts series -> /", "Industries served: Residential, Commercial, Restaurants, Interior Designers, Builders -> /", "Differentiator: marriage of design and function, attention to detail -> /about-us", "Award-winning knife block -> /", "Justin Penfield moved to Central Oregon in 2012 -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All of our designs are made in Bend, Oregon, created on site using our own woodworking, welding and fabrication skills", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='terrasteel-furniture-design-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
