UPDATE companies SET description='Texas Best Solar was founded in 2017 in Lewisville, Texas, by a Marine veteran and a custom home builder who shared a vision to change how North Texas homes and businesses generate power. The veteran-owned company began as a local response to rising energy costs and a desire for American-made solar solutions.

The firm provides turn-key solar installation, repair, and service across North Texas, handling design, product sourcing, and project execution. To date, the team has completed more than 400 installations, placing 8,750 panels and securing $2.7 million in customer incentives while saving an estimated 223 million kilowatt-hours.

Texas Best Solar serves residential and commercial customers throughout the region, offering systems that integrate with existing structures. The company sources panels from manufacturers such as Mission Solar Energy, prioritizing American-made and Texas-made products where possible.

The founders emphasize proper communication, setting clear expectations, and delivering a finished product that is both functionally and aesthetically proficient. They differentiate through ethically sourced, high-quality components and a customer-reference program that connects prospects with past clients.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar panel installation", "Solar system repair", "Solar maintenance service", "System design", "Product sourcing and procurement", "Turn-key project management", "Service call response", "Customer consultation"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Renewable energy"], "materials": ["Solar panels", "Mission Solar Energy panels"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["American-made first product sourcing", "Ethically sourced, high-quality components", "Transparent communication and expectation management", "Customer reference program", "Veteran-founded, North Texas focus"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2017 in Lewisville, Texas by Marine veteran and custom home builder -> /", "Veteran-owned -> /", "Solar installation, repair, and service provider in North Texas -> /", "8,750 solar panels placed, 400+ jobs completed, 223 million kWh saved, $2.7M incentives secured -> /", "Sources panels from Mission Solar Energy, prioritizes American-made and Texas-made products -> /", "Emphasizes proper communication, expectation setting, and functionally/aesthetically proficient finished product -> /", "Offers customer reference program -> /", "Headquarters: Lewisville, Texas -> db", "Website: http://www.texasbestsolar.com -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Solar Installation, Repair & Service in North Texas", "founded_year": "2017", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='texas-best-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Texas Capitol Semiconductor, Inc. (TCS) was founded in 1993 in Austin, Texas. The company now operates from Chandler, Arizona, and has been servicing the semiconductor industry for over 30 years.

Since its founding, TCS has remained at the forefront of high vacuum technology by specializing in the complexities of magnetic levitation technology and controller circuitry and software. The company services and repairs a broad range of turbomolecular (turbo) and cryogenic (cryo) pumps, offering complete service and repair for all turbo pumps and cryo pumps, as well as electronic controller service, technical and field service support 24/7, and rush repair service. Component-level repairs of turbo pump controllers and cryo onboard modules are also performed.

The company serves the semiconductor industry, providing vacuum pump repair solutions to semiconductor companies across North America and Europe.

