UPDATE companies SET description='The Fabric Cobbler operates a retail fabric and craft store in Forsyth, Illinois. The shop has been in business since at least 2007, as indicated by its copyright notice, and is run by the owner alongside her teenage children. The owner describes the venture as a personal endeavor born from a desire to create a welcoming community space.

The store carries a wide range of products including designer fabrics, precut fabric bundles, craft kits, notions, patterns, books, and needlework supplies. It also offers classes and events, as well as community programs such as a guild. The retail space is organized to allow customers to browse extensive fabric collections, and the owner emphasizes a curated selection that includes designs not commonly found in other shops.

The shop also sells online through its website and engages customers via live auctions on WhatNot and multiple social media channels.

The owner states that the shop was founded to provide a fully inclusive safe space for all people regardless of gender identity, sexual orientation, race, creed, or religion. An intersex- and BIPOC-inclusive flag is displayed in the window, and the owner has taken a public anti-MAGA stance, accepting the loss of some business as a consequence. Customers frequently cite the shop’s organization, unique fabric offerings, and the owner’s personal engagement as reasons for their loyalty.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail sales of designer fabrics", "Retail sales of craft kits and notions", "In-store sewing and craft classes", "Community event hosting", "Gift card sales", "Live auction sales via WhatNot", "Online retail via website"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fully inclusive safe space welcoming all gender identities, sexual orientations, races, creeds, and religions", "Public anti-MAGA stance and advocacy for marginalized communities", "Curated fabric selection featuring designs other shops decline to carry", "Organized retail layout praised by customers", "In-store classes, events, and community programs"], "facts_used": ["Location: 324 E. Ruehl Street, Forsyth, IL 62535 -> /", "Store hours: Mon-Tue 12-7, Wed-Sat 9-4 -> /", "Product categories: Books, Crafts, Fabrics, Gifts, Kits, Needle Arts, Notions, Patterns, Precuts -> /", "Owner mentions ''my teens and I'' and ''family'' -> /", "Inclusive safe space statement and anti-MAGA stance -> /", "Customer testimonials about organization and unique fabrics -> /", "Classes & Events, Programs, Guild mentioned -> /", "Copyright \u00a9 2007-2026 -> /", "Social media platforms listed (Facebook, Threads, Instagram, TikTok, WhatNot, YouTube, BlueSky, Substack, Pinterest, Upscrolled, Mastadon) -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Welcome to my shop! ... Categories: Book