The shop produces custom-built furniture, casegoods, and offers refinishing and restoration services. Every piece is hand-crafted by skilled artisans in the company''s Houston facility, allowing close control over design and construction. The operation focuses on one-of-a-kind items rather than volume production, with each project developed collaboratively.

The Joseph Company emphasizes its multi-generational expertise and the heirloom quality of its work, positioning each project as a collaborative effort that reflects the client''s vision while drawing on decades of family knowledge.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Built Furniture", "Casegoods", "Refinishing & Restoration"], "industries": ["Design Trade"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Exclusively serves the design trade", "Hand-crafted by skilled artisans in-house", "Family furniture-building heritage spanning over 70 years", "Custom pieces developed collaboratively with design partners", "Refinishing and restoration services available"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1990 -> db", "Headquartered in Houston, Texas -> db and page", "Family-owned heritage over 70 years -> page", "Exclusively serves the design trade -> page", "Hand-crafted by skilled artisans in own shop -> page", "Capabilities: Custom Built Furniture, Casegoods, Refinishing & Restoration -> db", "Industry served: Design Trade -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Each piece is hand crafted by our skilled artisans and made in our shop.", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-joseph-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The LYCRA Company operates its global headquarters in Waynesboro, Virginia, where it was founded in 1958.

The company manufactures a portfolio of branded fibers including LYCRA®, COOLMAX®, and THERMOLITE®, with recent additions made from pre‑consumer waste and partially renewable content. Beyond fiber production, it provides technical support for fabric processes such as knitting, weaving, and seamless construction, plus marketing assistance, product sourcing, and a digital platform (LYCRA ONE™) that enables fabric certification and virtual mill showrooms.

Its fibers are engineered for a wide range of garment categories: activewear, athleisure, bedding, denim, hosiery, intimates, personal care, ready‑to‑wear, socks, swimwear, and workwear. Customers include textile mills, apparel brands, and ultimately consumers seeking stretch, comfort, and durability.

