UPDATE companies SET description='The Little Potato Company is headquartered in DeForest, Wisconsin. The company traces its roots to 1996 when Angela and her father started with two shovels, a rented one-acre plot, and a dream in Canada. Canadian owned and operated since 1996, the business expanded to the United States in 2016, establishing American operations in Wisconsin. The company partners with family farms such as Coloma Farms, which has been operating since 1961, and growers like Steve who joined his family farm after college and has supplied the company since 2016.

The company specializes in growing, processing, packaging, and distributing small potato varieties. Working with a network of family farms across Canada and the U.S., it oversees planning, planting, growing, harvesting, and storing practices through its variety development team. The potatoes are packaged into consumer-ready products, including microwave-ready flavored lines such as Savory Herb and garlic and herb, and distributed to retail stores.

Its customers include busy families seeking convenient, fresh whole-food options, as evidenced by consumer testimonials. The company also partners with retail and office partners for distribution.

The business was built around family values—integrity, reliability, respect, and humility—and aims to create "little moments of happiness" for consumers. Sustainability is a core belief, reflected in responsible farmland use and generational partnerships with farming families.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Potato processing", "Packaging", "Distribution", "Variety development", "Sustainable farming practices", "Farm planning", "Planting", "Harvesting", "Storing"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Agriculture", "Food distribution", "Retail grocery"], "materials": ["Potatoes (multiple varieties)", "Herbs", "Spices"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Canadian owned and operated since 1996", "U.S. operations since 2016 with Wisconsin headquarters", "Longstanding partnerships with family farms in Canada and the U.S.", "Sustainability-focused farming practices", "Proprietary variety development for unique potato varieties"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in DeForest, Wisconsin -> db", "Founded in 1996 (Canadian owned and operated since 1996) -> /", "U.S. operations since 2016 -> /", "Partnership with Coloma Farms (operating since 1961) -> db", "Grower Steve supplying since 2016 -> db", "Processes: planning, planting, growing, harvesting, storing -> /about-us", "Variety development team -> /about-us", "Packaged products: Savory Herb Microwave Ready, garlic and herb, red little potatoes -> /", "Serves retail grocery and foodservice -> /", "Consumer testimonials from busy families -> /", "Core values: family, integrity, reliability, respect, humility -> /about-us", "Sustainability as core belief -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Potato Processing, Packaging, Distribution", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-little-potato-company-potato-processing-packaging-distribution' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Millwork Lab operates from a shop at 4420 NW 35th Court in Miami, Florida, producing custom architectural millwork, furniture, and cabinetry for residential and commercial projects. No founding year or ownership structure is publicly disclosed.

The company’s capabilities span custom woodwork, veneering with exotic laid veneers, and fabrication of fire-rated and solid-stock cores. Its output includes kitchen cabinets, commercial casework, custom furniture, decorative beams and columns, interior doors, wall and ceiling panels, elevator wood frames, and lobby and reception millwork. The shop emphasizes craftsmanship and machinery to create custom architectural profiles, though facility size and headcount are not disclosed. It works with a variety of wood species and applies finishes ranging from paints to specialized colors and styles.

The Millwork Lab serves architects, interior designers, general contractors, and homeowners across residential and commercial construction. Projects range from luxury home interiors to commercial lobby and reception areas, with the company highlighting its ability to meet client-specified time frames. The firm also offers design collaboration, working with clients or their designers to develop custom solutions.

The firm distinguishes itself through exotic custom laid veneers, a wide selection of woods, finishes, paints, and colors, and the capacity to deliver high-quality custom architectural profiles on schedule. It positions its production capabilities as a step above other woodworking shops in the Miami area.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom woodwork", "Architectural millwork", "Furniture making", "Wall panel fabrication", "Kitchen cabinet manufacturing", "Commercial casework", "Custom furniture", "Decorative beams and columns", "Interior door fabrication", "Wall and ceiling panel fabrication", "Elevator wood frames and panels", "Custom cabinetry", "Lobby and reception area millwork", "Veneering (exotic custom laid veneers)", "Fire-rated core fabrication", "Finish application (paints, colors, styles)", "Design collaboration"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Architecture", "Interior design", "General contracting"], "materials": ["Wood (various species)", "Veneers (exotic custom laid)", "Fire-rated cores", "Plywood", "Solid stock cores", "Paints", "Finishes"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Exotic custom laid veneers", "Fire-rated and solid-stock core options", "Custom architectural profiles crafted in-house", "Serves architects, designers, general contractors, and homeowners", "Meets client-specified time frames"], "facts_used": ["Location: Miami, FL (4420 NW 35th CT) -> /", "Services: architectural millwork, furniture, wall panels, kitchen cabinets, commercial casework -> /", "Customer types: architects, designers, general contractors, homeowners -> /", "Materials: exotic custom laid veneers, fire-rated cores, plywood, solid stock cores -> /", "Differentiators: exotic custom laid veneers, meet client time frames, custom architectural profiles -> /", "Contact email:  -> /", "Company description: carpenters as exceptional artisans -> /"], "company_t