UPDATE companies SET description='The Neil Jones Food Company is a family-run, privately-owned U.S. corporation headquartered in Vancouver, Washington. Founded in 1915 as San Benito Foods, the company began with a single can of premium San Benito tomatoes processed fresh from the field. The business has remained under family stewardship, with James Matthew Jones currently serving as CEO.

The company processes fresh-packed Pacific Northwest fruit — including pears, cherries, plums, and cranberries — and California tomato products such as canned tomatoes, pouches, custom sauces, and industrial varieties. It operates three processing facilities strategically located for national and international shipping. The Northwest Packing facility has canned Pacific Northwest fruit and produced industrial juices, purees, and blends since the 1970s. The TomaTek facility, built in the 1980s, specializes in aseptic technology for fresh-pack California tomatoes in industrial sizes and #10 equivalent pouches. All products are made in the U.S.A.

Customers span foodservice, industrial, retail, chain, and international channels. The company serves independent restaurants, school lunch programs, food manufacturers, chain restaurants, healthcare facilities, juice manufacturers, and cruise lines worldwide. Products appear under private label brands and in restaurants across the country.

The company emphasizes sustainable fresh-packing within hours of harvest, working closely with growers and agronomists to ensure quality ingredients. It highlights its commitment to not taking shortcuts, maintaining strict quality standards, and offering extensive customization capabilities for private label and foodservice partners.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fresh-pack processing", "Canning", "Aseptic processing", "Juice concentrate production", "Puree production", "Blend formulation", "Custom sauce formulation", "Pouch filling", "Industrial packaging", "Private label manufacturing"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Industrial food processing", "Retail", "Chain restaurants", "International export", "Food manufacturing", "Healthcare foodservice", "Juice manufacturing", "Cruise line catering", "Private label brands"], "materials": ["San Joaquin Valley tomatoes", "Pacific Northwest pears", "Pacific Northwest cherries", "Pacific Northwest plums", "Pacific Northwest cranberries"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Sustainable fresh-packing within hours of harvest", "Aseptic technology for shelf-stable tomato products", "Three strategically located processing facilities", "Custom product development for private label and foodservice", "Family-owned with multi-generational commitment"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1915 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Vancouver, Washington -> db", "Family-run, privately-owned U.S. Corporation -> /", "Three processing facilities strategically located -> /", "Northwest Packing facility canning since 1970s -> /about-us", "TomaTek facility built in 1980s with aseptic technology -> /about-us", "CEO James Matthew Jones -> /about-us", "Channels: foodservice, industrial, retail, chain, international -> /", "Customers: independent restaurants, schools, food manufacturers, chain restaurants, healthcare, juice manufacturers, cruise lines -> /about-us", "Customization capabiliti