UPDATE companies SET description='The Treehouse Hardwoods & Mill Shop was established in 1966 in South Burlington, Vermont. The business is operated by a team of woodworkers including Lucas, Carl, Jeremy, Adam, Tim, Sherb, John, and Jude, who together bring nearly 60 years of experience in buying, selling, and working with wood.

The company maintains a large inventory of domestic and exotic hardwoods, live-edge slabs sourced from Vermont, New Hampshire, and New York, hardwood plywood, and specialty items such as burls and "Hard Maple Cookies." Its millshop provides custom milling services including planing up to 24 inches, wide-belt sanding up to 42 inches, resawing up to 16 inches, CNC milling, and reproduction of antique moldings, car parts, and boat parts. The shop also produces butcher-block tops, table and counter tops, stair components, and custom sawn veneer.

Customers range from professional woodworkers and hobbyists to homeowners, builders, and contractors. The millshop handles small-to-medium projects, including new construction, remodeling, and historic building restoration.

The company distinguishes itself by combining a broad retail selection — described as the largest variety of hardwood plywood in northern Vermont — with a job-shop capable of custom reproduction work, all while emphasizing personal advice and service for projects of any skill level.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom millwork", "Butcherblock (edge, face, end-grain)", "Table tops, counter & island tops", "Stair treads, risers, skirts and nosing", "Custom threshold and transition strips", "Reproduction moldings", "Custom sawn veneer", "Planing (up to 24\")", "Wide belt sanding (up to 42\")", "Resawing (up to 16\")", "CNC milling", "Custom signs", "Wooden antique car part reproduction", "Antique moulding reproduction", "Custom boat part reproduction", "Retail sales of domestic and exotic hardwoods", "Live-edge slab selection", "Hardwood plywood sales", "Burl and specialty wood sales"], "industries": ["Woodworking", "Construction", "Remodeling", "Historic restoration", "Home improvement"], "materials": ["Domestic hardwoods", "Exotic hardwoods", "Hard maple", "Cherry", "Black walnut", "Hardwood plywood", "Burls", "Live-edge slabs"], "equipment": ["Planer (24\" capacity)", "Wide belt sander (42\" capacity)", "Resaw (16\" capacity)", "CNC milling machine"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest variety of hardwood plywood in northern Vermont", "Live-edge slabs sourced from Vermont, New Hampshire, and New York", "Custom millwork for historic building restoration", "CNC milling and custom reproduction of antique moldings, car parts, and boat parts"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1966 -> db", "Headquarters South Burlington, Vermont -> db, /", "Team members: Lucas, Carl, Jeremy, Adam, Tim, Sherb, John, Jude -> /", "Nearly 60 years of experience in buying, selling, and working with wood -> /", "Large inventory of domestic and exotic hardwoods, live-edge slabs, hardwood plywood, burls -> /", "Live-edge slabs sourced from Vermont, New Hampshire, New York -> /", "Largest variety of hardwood plywood in Northern VT -> /", "Millshop custom milling services: planing up to 24\", wide belt sanding up to 42\", resawing up to 16\" -> /services", "CNC milling, custom signs, antique car part reproduction, antique moulding reproduction, custom boat part reproduction -> /services", "Butcherblock, table tops, counter tops, stair treads, custom threshold strips, reproduction moldings, custom sawn veneer -> /services", "Shop rates: $85/hr general ($50 min), $120/hr specialty ($60 min) -> /services", "Serves professional woodworkers, hobbyists, homeowners, builders, contractors -> /, /services", "Projects: new construction, remodeling, historic building restoration -> /services", "Company type: contract manufacturer/job shop with retail sales -> /, /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We provide custom millwork for new construction, remodeling of current dwellings, and our favorite - restoration of historic buildings.", "founded_year": "1966", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-treehouse-hardwoods-mill-shop' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Wood Shop, Inc. operates from Orange City, Iowa, where it was founded in 1985 by DeWayne Dykstra. A family-owned business rooted in Dutch heritage, it began in a single-stall garage before moving to a dedicated facility in 1993. Dykstra passed ownership to his sons Josh, James, and Jake in 2018, who now lead a team of about 15 craftsmen and project managers.

The company manufactures custom cabinetry, architectural millwork, and fireplaces in its own woodworking shop, using mortise-and-tenon face frames, biscuit-joined construction, and furniture-grade finishes. It also provides full-service residential remodeling—kitchens, bathrooms, additions—and commercial cabinetry for offices, churches, schools, healthcare facilities, and retail spaces. Countertop materials include Cambria Quartz, granite, marble, onyx, solid surface, and laminate. Onyx Collection showers are fabricated and installed on-site.

Primary customers are homeowners across Northwest Iowa, including Orange City, Sioux Center, Le Mars, Okoboji, Sioux City, and surrounding communities. Commercial clients span offices, churches, schools, healthcare providers, and retail businesses throughout Iowa, with reach into South Dakota and Minnesota.

