UPDATE companies SET description='Thermoplastics Engineering Corporation was established in the summer of 1986 in Leominster, Massachusetts. The company operated independently for over three decades before being acquired in June 2021 by Broomfield, a fourth-generation family-owned winding machine manufacturer based in Bolton, Massachusetts.

The company engineers and builds custom machinery for wire, cable, and fiber optic production. Its product lines include extruders, cablers, respoolers, payoffs, takeups, dancers, accumulators, capstans, control systems, and taping equipment. TEC also serves the plastics market with machinery for tubing, profile, and compounding extrusion. A multidisciplinary staff of mechanics, engineers, electricians, programmers, and machinists supports design, fabrication, and service.

TEC serves manufacturers in the wire and cable, fiber optic, and plastics extrusion sectors. Its equipment is used in the production of insulated wire, fiber optic cable, plastic tubing, profile shapes, and compounded materials. The company provides both complete production lines and individual machines to integrate into existing operations.

TEC differentiates itself by starting with a base machine platform and customizing it to each customer''s unique requirements. The company emphasizes its experienced in-house team and its ability to deliver end-to-end solutions for fiber optic cable products, as well as its commitment to building dependable machines for the wire and cable production process.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom extrusion line engineering", "Wire cabling machinery", "Cable extrusion machinery", "Fiber optic cable manufacturing machinery", "Tubing extrusion machinery", "Profile extrusion machinery", "Compounding machinery", "Control systems for extrusion lines", "Dancer/accumulator/capstan systems", "Taping equipment", "Payoff and takeup systems", "Respooling equipment"], "industries": ["Wire and cable", "Fiber optic", "Plastics extrusion", "Tubing extrusion", "Profile extrusion", "Compounding"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Extruders", "Cablers", "Respoolers", "Payoffs", "Takeups", "Dancers", "Accumulators", "Capstans", "Control systems", "Taping equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Base machine platforms customized to unique customer requirements", "Multidisciplinary in-house staff (mechanics, engineers, electricians, programmers, machinists)", "End-to-end solutions for fiber optic cable manufacturing", "Focus on dependable machinery for wire and cable production"], "facts_used": ["Founded summer 1986 in Leominster, MA -> /about", "Acquired by Broomfield in June 2021 -> /about", "Broomfield is a fourth-generation family-owned winding machine company -> /about", "Specializes in custom machinery for cable extrusion and wire coating extrusion -> /", "Product lines: Wire Cablers, Control Systems, Dancers, Accumulators & Capstans, Cable Extruders, Taping, Fiber Optic & Misc., Payoffs & Takeups -> /", "Serves wire and cable, fiber optic, tubing, profile, compounding markets -> /about", "Staff includes mechanics, engineers, electricians, programmers, machinists -> /about", "Vision: build dependable machines for wire & cable production process -> /", "Custom engineering of base machines to unique customer requirements -> /", "End-to-end solution for fiber optic cable products -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in engineering custom machinery for the cable extrusion and wire coating extrusion process.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='thermoplastics-engineering-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Thexton Manufacturing Co. has operated from Edina, Minnesota since its founding in 1907.

The company designs and manufactures a range of professional automotive tools, including electrical and battery tools, diagnostic and fuel system testers, terminal tools, cooling system tools, brake tools, and lubrication equipment. Production takes place in a 20,000-square-foot facility that houses a machine shop, an R&D department with CAD capabilities, an electronic design and assembly area, and a complete packaging line. Thexton introduces 10 to 20 new products each year, developed by an in-house engineering team that includes Senior Product Development Engineer Josh Oachs.

Thexton serves the automotive aftermarket, selling through a network of distributors to professional mechanics and technicians. Its catalog targets repair shops and technicians who need specialized tools for hard-to-find repairs.

