UPDATE companies SET description='Tigon Medical is based in Millersville, Maryland. The company was founded in 2017 by Jeremy Clark, who set out to deliver innovative suture anchors while addressing the single-use plastic waste generated by many surgical procedures. This sustainability focus became the core of Tigon’s mission.

The company designs and sells surgical implants, instruments, and suture for the sports medicine market. Its product lines include knotted and knotless suture anchors (such as the Manticore, Tomahawk, Javelin, and Dual Infiniti families), suture products (TigoLoop, TigoTape, TigoCable), the Fire System, Flyer, biologics (Vampire Awl, TigoDerm), and dedicated instrument sets for shoulder, foot and ankle, and bicep procedures. Tigon received clearance to market its products in 2019 and has since expanded into labral and rotator cuff surgeries. The team includes engineering, quality and regulatory, and sales personnel.

The company says its GreenRepair® initiative sets it apart by minimizing waste across all surgical procedures, while its broader goal is to improve patient outcomes and surgeon performance through innovative implant and instrument design.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surgical implant design", "Surgical instrument design", "Suture anchor development", "Suture product development", "Biologics product development", "Instrument set design", "Quality and regulatory compliance", "Product development engineering"], "industries": ["Sports medicine", "Orthopedic surgery", "Shoulder surgery", "Foot and ankle surgery"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["GreenRepair\u00ae sustainability program to reduce single-use plastic waste", "Innovative suture anchor designs for knotless and knotted repairs", "Focus on improving patient outcomes and surgeon performance", "Product portfolio covering shoulder and foot/ankle sports medicine", "In-house engineering, quality, and regulatory expertise"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Millersville, Maryland -> db", "Founded in 2017 by Jeremy Clark -> /about-us", "Mission to minimize waste and develop suture anchors -> /about-us", "Received clearance to market products in 2019 -> /about-us", "Expanded into labral and rotator cuff surgeries, introduced GreenRepair\u00ae -> /about-us", "Designs and sells surgical implants, instruments, suture for sports medicine -> /", "Product lines: anchors (knotted, knotless), suture (TigoLoop, TigoTape, TigoCable), Fire System, Flyer, biologics (Vampire Awl, TigoDerm), instrument sets -> /", "Procedures: shoulder (rotator cuff, labral repair, instability, biceps repair), foot & ankle (Achilles, Brostrom) -> /", "Team members: Jeremy Clark (President/Founder), Zac Sullivan (Director of Sales), Sam Homick (Northeast Regional Sales Director), Melinda Tiao (Engineering & Project Manager, Quality & Regulatory Manager), Matias Ng (Product Development Engineer), Gina Royster (Contracts/Distribution Control), Ryan Pratt (Sales Representative) -> /about-us", "Certification: ROHS -> db", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Tigon Medical \u2013 Designs and sells surgical implants, instruments and suture for the sports medicine industry.", "founded_year": "2017", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/tigonmedical/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tigon-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Timber Woodworking Machinery, Inc. operates from a 33,000-square-foot facility on three acres in Mesa, Arizona. The company was founded in 1989 by Charles and Paulette Larson after they struggled to find quality tools and supplies for their own woodworking projects. The Larsons opened their first store in a 2,700-square-foot strip mall on East Southern Avenue, and the business grew steadily. In 2005, their daughter RaeAnn Yoder and son-in-law Mel Yoder assumed control of the machinery division, and when the founders retired in 2010, the couple also took over the lumber side of the operation.

The retailer stocks a broad range of woodworking tools, equipment, and supplies, including hardwood lumber, used machinery, used parts, carbide router bits, and sharpening services. Its showroom spans roughly 13,000 square feet and displays products from brands such as Amana, Bosch, CMT, Freud, Delta, Jet, Powermatic, and others. The company also runs a consignment program that allows customers to sell their own used equipment through the store.

Customers include commercial cabinet shops, custom furniture manufacturers, and home-shop hobbyists across the Southwest. The business serves both large production operations and individual woodworkers, offering everything from hand carving tools to large production machines.

